      {
        "user": "the GIL means Python can't do parallelism at all, right?",
        "ai": "No, that's not right. The Global Interpreter Lock (GIL) prevents true *thread* parallelism in single-core Python, but it doesn't stop parallelism at all\u2014you can still run code across multiple cores using the `multiprocessing` module or by leveraging C extensions that release the lock.",
        "route": "fast",
        "lang": "en",
        "ack": "",
        "injected": 0,
        "actions": [],
        "pending": [],
        "ttft_ms": 8261.952690999351,
