      },
      {
        "user": "no I'm pretty sure it can't",
        "ai": "Actually, you're mixing up threads and processes. The GIL only blocks multi-threaded CPU-bound code from running simultaneously on the same core, but Python can still achieve parallelism using multiple *processes* (via `multiprocessing`) or libraries like `concurrent.futures` that manage processes internally. Threads aren't the only way to parallelize!",
        "route": "fast",
        "lang": "en",
